  "changes": [
    "The .Sound driver body is absent from the supplied source release. The restored 288 instructions implement opening, closing, control, square-wave playback, four-tone synthesis, free-form sample playback, and vertical-blank scheduling. Labels without a recorded source or Ghidra name describe reconstructed behavior.",
    "Original SysEqu.a, ToolUtils.a, Private.a, HardwareEqu.a, and Traps.a declarations identify low-memory globals, driver fields, timer registers, VIA ports, and VBL calls. Hardware declarations use the Macintosh Plus conditional section.",
    "PatchPlusROM.a identifies DoneVBL at $417B50, ROMBMap at $417C82, FmBMapStart at $417C84, and the ends of DeAlloc and DoneVBL. Its December 1985 comment is preserved as a historical follow-up.",
    "The original queue defects remain: InstallVBL clears the queue link before checking SoundActive; ROMBMap returns on an empty queue without removing its task; and CheckBMapQueue calls DoneVBL when a request finishes. Later patch replacements are not included.",
    "The header uses named entry offsets and the resource catalog master-pointer offset. ORI.B #192 retains the zero high byte of the immediate extension word; a signed -64 spelling would assemble differently with this GNU assembler."
  ],
